course: dictionary
lesson: 7129
title: Penance: saying sorry and making up for it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from one subject, such as church, and penance is one of them. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «On Saturday he went to confession at church.» Confession is telling your wrongs to a priest, so penance must come after it.
explain: «The priest listened, gave him absolution and a small penance, a short prayer or task to show he is sorry.» The sentence tells you what a penance is: a small thing you do to show you are sorry. Try your meaning in the sentence: the priest gave him a small way to show he is sorry. It still makes sense.
explain: Penance can also mean something unpleasant you have to put up with, as if it were a punishment. «Waiting in the queue was a penance.» Swap in punishment: waiting in the queue was a punishment. That fits, so this is the everyday meaning.
fact: Penance means something you do to show you are sorry for a wrong or a sin.
fact: In the Catholic Church, penance is often given after confession, and it is often a few prayers.
fact: Penance is also the name of the sacrament of confession, which is also called reconciliation.
fact: «Do penance» means doing something hard to make up for a wrong.
fact: «Waiting in the queue was a penance» means waiting was so unpleasant it felt like a punishment.
exercise: «The priest gave him a small penance, a short prayer.» What is a penance here? | *Something you do to show you are sorry | A new coat for winter | A kind of church bell | A bag of sweets
exercise: «On Saturday he went to confession at church.» What comes just after confession in the Catholic Church? | *A penance | A football match | A birthday party | A school trip
exercise: «Waiting in the queue was a penance.» What does penance suggest here? | Something unpleasant you have to put up with | *Something unpleasant you have to put up with, like a punishment | A happy surprise | A cold drink on a hot day
test: «The priest said he was forgiven and asked him to put the coin back as penance.» What word means the same as forgiven here? | Dusty | Hungry | Lost | *Pardoned
test: «He had to do penance by saying sorry to the lollipop lady.» What does do penance mean? | Sing a song loudly | Win a prize | Go shopping | *Do something hard to make up for a wrong
exam: Jayden asks, «What is the sacrament of penance?» Which answer is right? | Yes, it is the name of a church building | It is a kind of sweet | It is a type of football game | *It is the name of confession, also called reconciliation
